module scd-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frcp6.{ frcp6 }

// The District of South Carolina's own periods, computed under the federal
// rules (FRCP 6(a) governs "any local rule"). The rules are cited as
// "Local Civ. Rule __ (D.S.C.)" (Local Civ. Rule 1.01). Absent an exception
// granted by the court, an initial memorandum is limited to 35 and a reply
// to 15 double-spaced pages (Local Civ. Rule 7.05(B)); they are not
// declared as `limit`s, whose cite check reads "thirty-five (35) pages"
// with no word between the count and the measure. A party may grant in
// writing one extension of the time to respond to a pleading, of at most
// the lesser of 21 days or the original response period (Local Civ. Rule
// 12.01). A stipulated extension of a written discovery response may not
// place its due date less than 30 days before the end of the discovery
// period (Local Civ. Rules 29.01, 37.01(A)). Witnesses identified within
// the last 28 days of the discovery period are presumed untimely absent
// good cause (Local Civ. Rule 16.02(D)(2)). A mediation memorandum the
// mediator requires should be no more than 5 pages unless the mediator
// permits (Local Civ. Rule 16.08(B)). A bond staying execution of a
// money-only judgment is 150% of a judgment of $10,000 or less and 125% of
// a larger one (Local Civ. Rule 62.01(A)). The scheduling order itself
// issues within the FRCP 16(b)(2) period, which is lit/frcp's. The earlier
// District of South Carolina outline's FRCP flow and its decisions
// (Twombly, Iqbal, Foman, Frow, Celotex, Anderson v. Liberty Lobby,
// Catlin, Bowles) are FRCP or FRAP authority and belong to lit/frcp; its
// Third Circuit decisions (Phillips, Fowler, Poulis) do not bind this
// district, and its Fourth Circuit decisions (Goines; Anderson v.
// Foundation for Advancement) are vendored nowhere, so they are removed.
/// A pleading asserting a claim is filed (Local Civ. Rule 4.01).
event ComplaintFiled()
/// A motion is served (Local Civ. Rules 7.04, 7.06).
event MotionServed()
/// A response to a motion is served (Local Civ. Rules 7.06, 7.07).
event ResponseServed()
/// Counsel receive a proposed order submitted to the court (Local Civ.
/// Rule 7.10(B)(4)-(5)).
event ProposedOrderReceived()
/// A defendant appears (Local Civ. Rules 16.01(A), 16.02(C)(1)).
event DefendantAppeared()
/// The parties hold the FRCP 26(f) conference (Local Civ. Rule 16.02(C)).
event PartiesConferred()
/// The discovery period set by the scheduling order closes (Local Civ.
/// Rules 16.02(D)(3), 26.04).
event DiscoveryClosed()
/// An affidavit of a records custodian is served (Local Civ. Rule
/// 16.02(D)(3)).
event CustodianAffidavitServed()
/// The deadline for mediation arrives (Local Civ. Rule 16.06(C)).
event MediationDeadlineReached()
/// The parties agree on a mediator or the court appoints one (Local Civ.
/// Rule 16.07(A)).
event MediatorAppointed()
/// A mediation conference is held (Local Civ. Rules 16.07(A), 16.08(D)).
event MediationConferenceHeld()
/// The mediation concludes (Local Civ. Rule 16.10(H)).
event MediationConcluded()
/// A notice of removal is served (Local Civ. Rule 26.01).
event RemovalNoticeServed()
/// The clerk draws a party's failure to file the Local Civ. Rule 26.01
/// answers to its attention (Local Civ. Rule 26.01).
event InterrogatoryAnswersNoticeGiven()
/// Issues are joined in an action exempt under FRCP 26(a)(1)(B) (Local
/// Civ. Rule 26.04).
event IssueJoined()
/// The date set for jury selection, the trial date for scheduling (Local
/// Civ. Rules 16.02(B), 26.05).
event JurySelected()
/// The date set for submitting pretrial briefs (Local Civ. Rule 26.07(A)).
event PretrialBriefsDue()
/// Trial begins (Local Civ. Rule 26.09).
event TrialCommenced()
/// The date on which the action is scheduled for trial (Local Civ. Rule
/// 54.01).
event TrialDateScheduled()
/// A deposition is taken (Local Civ. Rule 30.02).
event DepositionTaken()
/// A deposition is suspended or terminated over an instruction not to
/// answer (Local Civ. Rule 30.04(C)).
event DepositionSuspended()
/// A discovery response is received (Local Civ. Rule 37.01(A)).
event DiscoveryResponseReceived()
/// A discovery response comes due and none is received (Local Civ. Rule
/// 37.01(A)).
event DiscoveryResponseOverdue()
/// A petition for attorney's fees is served (Local Civ. Rule 54.02(A)).
event FeePetitionServed()
/// A motion to withdraw that would leave the party unrepresented is filed
/// (Local Civ. Rule 83.I.07(B)).
event WithdrawalMotionFiled()
/// The clerk posts notice of intent to dispose of exhibits (Local Civ. Rule
/// 83.II.01).
event ExhibitDisposalNoticePosted()
/// The Social Security Administration has issued all notices of award of
/// benefits (Local Civ. Rule 83.VII.10(A)).
event AwardNoticesIssued()

/// Local Civ. Rule 4.01: if a pleading asserting a claim is not served on
/// each party against whom a claim is asserted within 90 days after it is
/// filed, the filer files a status report within the same period.
deadline service-status-report-period: 90.days after ComplaintFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 4.01"
/// Local Civ. Rule 7.06: a memorandum or response of an opposing party is
/// filed within 14 days of the service of the motion unless the court
/// imposes a different deadline.
deadline response-period: 14.days after MotionServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 7.06"
/// Local Civ. Rule 7.07: replies are discouraged; a reply to matters raised
/// initially in a response is filed within 7 days after service of the
/// response, unless otherwise ordered.
deadline reply-period: 7.days after ResponseServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 7.07"
/// Local Civ. Rule 7.10(B)(5): unless otherwise ordered, opposing counsel
/// have 14 days from receipt to comment on a proposed order.
deadline proposed-order-comment-period: 14.days after ProposedOrderReceived() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 7.10(B)"
/// Local Civ. Rule 16.02(C)(1): the FRCP 26(f) conference is held no later
/// than 45 days after the appearance of a defendant.
deadline rule26f-conference-period: 45.days after DefendantAppeared() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 16.02(C)"
/// Local Civ. Rule 16.02(C)(2): the FRCP 26(a)(1) initial disclosures are
/// exchanged no later than 14 days after the FRCP 26(f) conference.
deadline initial-disclosure-period: 14.days after PartiesConferred() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 16.02(C)"
/// Local Civ. Rule 16.02(C)(3): the FRCP 26(f) report is filed no later
/// than 14 days after the FRCP 26(f) conference.
deadline rule26f-report-period: 14.days after PartiesConferred() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 16.02(C)"
/// Local Civ. Rule 16.02(D)(3): affidavits of records custodians offered
/// for authentication in lieu of live testimony are served no fewer than
/// 30 days before the close of discovery unless otherwise ordered.
deadline custodian-affidavit-period: 30.days before DiscoveryClosed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 16.02(D)"
/// Local Civ. Rule 16.02(D)(3): objections to a records custodian's
/// affidavit are made within 14 days after service of the disclosure
/// unless otherwise ordered.
deadline custodian-objection-period: 14.days after CustodianAffidavitServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 16.02(D)"
/// Local Civ. Rule 16.06(C): unless otherwise ordered, the parties select a
/// mediator at least 21 days before the deadline for mediation.
deadline mediator-selection-period: 21.days before MediationDeadlineReached() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 16.06(C)"
/// Local Civ. Rule 16.07(A): unless otherwise ordered, the initial
/// mediation conference is held within 28 days of the agreement upon or
/// order appointing a mediator.
deadline initial-mediation-period: 28.days after MediatorAppointed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 16.07(A)"
/// Local Civ. Rule 16.07(A): unless otherwise ordered, mediation is
/// completed within 28 days after the initial mediation conference.
deadline mediation-completion-period: 28.days after MediationConferenceHeld() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 16.07(A)"
/// Local Civ. Rule 16.08(D): a more formal agreement the mediated
/// settlement envisions is executed by the parties within 14 days of the
/// date of the mediation conference.
deadline settlement-documents-period: 14.days after MediationConferenceHeld() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 16.08(D)"
/// Local Civ. Rule 16.10(H): the mediator forwards the completed ADR
/// tracking form within 28 days of the conclusion of the mediation.
deadline mediator-report-period: 28.days after MediationConcluded() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 16.10(H)"
/// Local Civ. Rule 26.01: in a removed case the removing defendant files
/// the Local Civ. Rule 26.01 answers with the removal papers; every other
/// party files them no later than 14 days after service of the notice of
/// removal.
deadline removal-interrogatory-answers-period: 14.days after RemovalNoticeServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 26.01"
/// Local Civ. Rule 26.01: a party that fails to file the answers on time is
/// allowed 14 days to file them after the clerk draws the requirement to
/// its attention; the clerk may extend the time.
deadline late-interrogatory-answers-period: 14.days after InterrogatoryAnswersNoticeGiven() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 26.01"
/// Local Civ. Rule 26.04: pretrial discovery in an action exempt under
/// FRCP 26(a)(1)(B) is completed within 90 days following the joinder of
/// issues unless otherwise ordered.
deadline exempt-discovery-period: 90.days after IssueJoined() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 26.04"
/// Local Civ. Rule 26.04: in an exempt action, FRCP 26(a)(2) expert
/// disclosures are made at least 28 days before the close of discovery.
deadline exempt-expert-disclosure-period: 28.days before DiscoveryClosed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 26.04"
/// Local Civ. Rule 26.05: a pretrial brief is furnished at least 7 days
/// before the date set for jury selection, unless the court orders another
/// date.
deadline pretrial-brief-period: 7.days before JurySelected() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 26.05"
/// Local Civ. Rule 26.05(O): requests for voir dire questions not submitted
/// 7 days before jury selection are waived unless events at trial make them
/// necessary.
deadline voir-dire-request-period: 7.days before JurySelected() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 26.05(O)"
/// Local Civ. Rule 26.07(A): unless otherwise ordered, counsel meet to mark
/// and exchange trial exhibits at least 7 days before the date set for
/// submitting pretrial briefs.
deadline exhibit-exchange-period: 7.days before PretrialBriefsDue() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 26.07(A)"
/// Local Civ. Rule 26.09: requests for jury instructions are submitted 7
/// days before the beginning of trial, or are waived unless events at
/// trial make them necessary.
deadline jury-instruction-period: 7.days before TrialCommenced() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 26.09"
/// Local Civ. Rule 30.02: a party objecting to a telephonic deposition
/// makes the objection known at least 14 days before the deposition.
deadline telephone-deposition-objection-period: 14.days before DepositionTaken() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 30.02"
/// Local Civ. Rule 30.04(C): counsel who directs a witness not to answer,
/// other than on privilege or to enforce a court-ordered limitation, moves
/// for a protective order within 7 days of the suspension or termination
/// of the deposition, or waives the objection.
deadline deposition-protective-order-period: 7.days after DepositionSuspended() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 30.04(C)"
/// Local Civ. Rule 37.01(A): a motion to compel is filed within 21 days
/// after receipt of the discovery response it is directed to.
deadline motion-to-compel-period: 21.days after DiscoveryResponseReceived() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 37.01(A)"
/// Local Civ. Rule 37.01(A): where no response has been received, a motion
/// to compel is filed within 21 days after the response was due.
deadline motion-to-compel-no-response-period: 21.days after DiscoveryResponseOverdue() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 37.01(A)"
/// Local Civ. Rule 54.01: juror costs may be assessed when a case set for
/// jury trial is settled or disposed of before trial unless the court is
/// notified at least one day before the date the action is scheduled for
/// trial.
deadline jury-cost-notice-period: 1.days before TrialDateScheduled() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 54.01"
/// Local Civ. Rule 54.02(A): a memorandum opposing a petition for
/// attorney's fees is filed within 14 days of the service of the petition.
deadline fee-opposition-period: 14.days after FeePetitionServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 54.02(A)"
/// Local Civ. Rule 83.I.07(B)(3): a party to be left unrepresented by
/// counsel's withdrawal is told that any response must be received within
/// 17 days of the filing date of the motion.
deadline withdrawal-response-period: 17.days after WithdrawalMotionFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 83.I.07(B)"
/// Local Civ. Rule 83.II.01: unless an attorney of record or party in
/// interest takes custody of or objects within 14 days of the posting of
/// the clerk's notice, the clerk may dispose of the exhibits as stated.
deadline exhibit-disposal-objection-period: 14.days after ExhibitDisposalNoticePosted() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 83.II.01"
/// Local Civ. Rule 83.VII.10(A): a petition for attorney's fees out of
/// past-due Social Security benefits is filed no later than 60 days after
/// the issuance of all notices of award of benefits; the United States
/// Attorney is allowed 30 days to object (83.VII.10(C)), a period the rule
/// gives no start for, so it is not declared.
deadline ssa-fee-petition-period: 60.days after AwardNoticesIssued() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 83.VII.10(A)"

test "service status report period: 90 days after the trigger" cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 4.01"
{
  given ComplaintFiled() on 2026-11-02
  expect deadline(service-status-report-period) == 2027-02-01
}

test "response period: 14 days after the trigger" cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 7.06"
{
  given MotionServed() on 2026-11-02
  expect deadline(response-period) == 2026-11-16
}

test "reply period: 7 days after the trigger" cite "D.S.C. Local Civ. Rule 7.07"
{
  given ResponseServed() on 2026-11-02
  expect deadline(reply-period) == 2026-11-09
}

